 ],
 "notes": "Photos 00-02 (exteriors) and the interior views: a two-storey grey concrete house on a flat suburban lot with a lawn and stepping-stone path. Upper storey a white rendered box (about 11 x 7 m) with concrete bands at floor and roof and tall vertical windows; below it, the ground floor is a lattice of hollow concrete blocks on the west (the open breeze-block screen), a dark entrance bay and dark recess. On the garden side a deep exposed-concrete canopy runs the full width over a covered terrace with a timber table, glazed living room behind it, a block wall at the east end, and a planted open patio (the 'intermediate space' of the article) cut through the slab and filled with big-leaf plants. Round 1 had the white box too big and the patio missing; round 2 cut the patio and shrank the box; round 3 enlarged the patio so its plants read from above, thinned the concrete bands so the upper box reads white, added a cable rail on the roof deck; the canopy edge was also lowered and added the block screen walls and stepping stones. Guessed: which side is north, overall plan size, the roof terrace rail (photo 02 shows a roof deck with a cable rail on the east), position and size of the patio, neighbours (drawn only as two plain blocks), the interior stair. Placed at its town only (Buenos Aires)."
}